Parades march down the street, providing a distraction for those waiting in line for the carnival rides. By Saturday October 9, 1999, the Fuengirola Fair was entering its third day and it was still as popular as ever. That night, a taxi driver dropped some passengers off in the Fuengirola area before heading south-west towards the coastal village of La Cala de Mijas. As he drove along a quiet, rural stretch of road between towns, he eyed his meter. It was exactly ten p.m. Suddenly, an SUV appeared up ahead.
